/*****************************************************************************
    kant8M1o -- M1's INTERPRETED COLUMN, IN ITS OWN PROCESS. 2026-08-10.

    Same body as kant8M1, interpreted only. Its own process for the reason
    recorded on jitJRt2o. A post-jit interpreted call is not a clean oracle
    for a returned value, because whether the frame bracket runs depends on
    invocation history.

    This file records a DIVERGENCE and not an agreement, in the manner of
    jitJRt3o. If the interpreted column ever starts agreeing with the jitted
    one, that is the KANT-8 repair landing, and this row is what says so.

    GRADUATED 2026-08-10, SEQ 27 rung A. It said so. The interpreted column
    now returns the value rather than the tag, because the return seam in
    runAction takes the result value before the restore sweep runs, so the
    caller no longer receives a pointer into the frame being restored. The
    printed expectation below has been moved to match, and the old reading is
    named there as the regression so a return of the tag stays legible as one.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT, exactly ONE stop.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(Kant8M1o);
define
    m1n;
    m1out;
    m1 code={
        m1count = m1n + 40;
        m1text  = "alive";
        print "M1 int  before  : m1count =" m1count " m1text =" m1text:;
        if m1n > 0;
            m1n = m1n - 1;
            m1();
        print "M1 int  after   : m1count =" m1count " m1text =" m1text:;
        return m1count;
        };
    ;

m1n = 2;
m1out = m1();
print "M1 int  returned: m1out =" m1out " (want 42; the TAG m1count = KANT-8 is back)":;

print "M1o SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
